/3). It builds on #23 (`assess-stamped`, `align-stamped`, still open), which lands first on its own, and on #16 (merged): its report conventions and the \"Skill versions\" rule.\n\nThe skills are developed against concrete use cases. Agents run them on a ladder of ds007116 tasks in fresh containers, and the resulting projects are graded outside the sandbox, by scripted probes, private reference tables and fresh-clone reruns.\n\nDocs only; there are no skills or code yet.\n\n## Files\n\n- `docs/stamped/PLAN.md`: the skills and their names, design principles, layering and layout, answer format, roadmap with per-PR obligations, risks, and decisions and open questions.\n- `docs/stamped/evals.md`: use cases R0–R2 (with R1, brain extraction on 10 named subjects, as the main target), pilots, arms, runners and sandbox rules, grading (external vs self-assessed), calibration, iteration protocol, publishing, budget and done criteria.\n- `docs/stamped/prior-work.md`: sources.\n- `docs/stamped/stack-repronim.md`: draft ReproNim stack reference.\n- `docs/stamped/talks.md`: how this feeds the MIT and US-RSE talks (con/talks#33).\n\n## Status\n\nDraft for discussion. Four review rounds and @asmacdo's notes are addressed (f25257e, 4a18324, 3f5a560, f351632), and `master` was merged in after #16 landed; open decisions are in PLAN §8. The plan is to squash before this leaves draft, or to squash-merge. con/skills has no PR template or contributing guide. The validator workflow does not run on docs-only changes; `ci/validate_skills.py` passes locally (0 errors).\n\n## Handoff: starting phase 1b/2 on a controlled host\n\nFor a Claude Code session continuing there:\n\n1. Work from branch `claude/ecstatic-cerf-nh4j6w`, or branch off it.\n2. Check the host: Apptainer, scratch space (R1 needs a few GB per image), the Claude CLI, and `uv`.\n3. Install the pinned runner tooling and record it under `evals/stamped/`:\n   - `datalad` (a release with the gh-7899 fix);\n   - `datalad-container`;\n   - `git-annex` (the PyPI wheel works);\n   - `con-duct`.\n4. Bootstrap the results dataset (`datalad create -c text2git`), add con/skills as a subdataset, and add the hub siblings, private first.\n5. Follow PLAN §6 from the current phase.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_018TvTLThBRhJrk8ZZtGVFNb","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T06:02:27Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"79d46f34a9fa84d76b3e3b5dec27abd2611654b3","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"con:claude/ecstatic-cerf-nh4j6w","ref":"claude/ecstatic-cerf-nh4j6w","repo":{"id":1162654830,"node_id":"R_kgDORUy0bg","name":"skills","full_name":"con/skills","owner":{"login":"con","id":13295221,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEzMjk1MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13295221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/con","html_url":"https://github.com/con","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Anthropics claude-code skills for the CON masses","homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":4,"forks":4,"stargazers_